{"r":"TrH","lane":{"p":1837,"e":[{"h":"طَرَحَهُ","t":["and ",[2,"طَرَحَ بِهِ"],", (S, A, Mgh, O, Msb, K,) the latter allowable because a verb that is syn. with another verb may have the same government as the latter, and ",[2,"طَرَحَ"]," is syn. with a verb that is trans. by means of ",[2,"ب"],", as will be shown in what follows, (Msb,) aor. , (Mgh, Msb, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"طَرْحٌ"],", (S, Mgh, O, Msb,) ",[1,"He cast it, threw it,"]," or ",[1,"flung it;"]," or ",[1,"cast, threw,"]," or ",[1,"flung, it away;"]," [and particularly ",[1,"as a thing of no account;"]," (see ",[2,"طِرْحٌ"],";)] syn. ",[2,"رَمَاهُ"],", (S, A, O, K,) or ",[2,"رَمَى بِهِ"],", (Mgh, Msb,) and ",[2,"أَلْقَاهُ"],"; (A, Mgh;) ",[2,"مِنْ يَدِهِ"]," [",[1,"from his hand"],"]. (Mgh.) You say, ",[2,"طَرَحَ لَهُ"],[2,"الوِسَادَةَ"]," (A, TA) ",[1,"He threw to him the pillow,"]," or ",[1,"cushion;"]," syn. ",[2,"أَلْقَاهُ"],". (TA.) And ",[2,"طَرَحْتُ الرِّدَآءَ"],[2,"عَلَى عَاتِقِى"],[1,"I threw the"]," [",[1,"garment called"],"] ",[2,"ردآء"],[1,"upon my shoulder;"]," syn. ",[2,"أَلْقَيْتُهُ"],". (Msb.) And [hence] ",[2,"طَرَحَ عَلَيْهِ المَسْأَلَةَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He put,"]," or ",[1,"proposed,"]," (lit. ",[1,"threw,"],") ",[1,"to him the question:"]," (A, * TA:) thought by ISd to be post-classical. (TA.) [And in post-classical language, ",[2,"طَرحٌ"]," signifies also The ",[1,"making a throw"]," in the game of backgammon and the like; and the ",[1,"making a move"]," in the game of chess &c.] ― -b2- Also, i. e. ",[2,"طَرَحَهُ"]," and ",[2,"طَرَحَ بِهِ"],", ",[1,"He removed it; placed it,"]," or ",[1,"put it, at a distance; put it away,"]," or ",[1,"far away;"]," [",[1,"cast it off, rejected it,"]," or ",[1,"discarded it;"],"] (ISd, K, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"اِطَّرَحَهُ"],"; (S, A, O, K;) [respecting which see 8 in art. ",[2,"ضرح"],";] and ↓ ",[2,"طرّحهُ"],", (K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَطْرِيحٌ"],"; (TA;) or this last signifies ",[1,"he cast it, threw it,"]," or ",[1,"flung it,"]," or ",[1,"he cast, threw,"]," or ",[1,"flung, it away, much,"]," or ",[1,"frequently."]," (S, A, O.) One says, ",[2,"طَرَحَتِ النَّوَى بِفُلَانٍ كُلَّ مَطْرَحٍ"]," i. e. (tropical:) [",[1,"Removal,"]," or ",[1,"distance,"]," or ",[1,"the place to which he journeyed,"],"] ",[1,"rendered such a one"]," [",[1,"utterly"],"] ",[1,"remote"]," [or ",[1,"cast away"],"]. (S, O, TA. [Here ",[2,"مَطْرَح"]," is an inf. n.]) And [in like manner] ",[2,"طَرَحَ بِهِ الدَّهْرُ كُلَّ"],[2,"مَطْرَحٍ"]," i. e. (tropical:) [",[1,"Time,"]," or ",[1,"fortune,"],"] ",[1,"removed him,"]," or ",[1,"separated him,"]," [",[1,"utterly,"],"] ",[1,"from his family and kindred."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"مَا طَرَحَكَ إِلَى هٰذِهِ البِلَادِ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"What has driven thee to these regions?"],"]. (A.) And ",[2,"اِطْرَحْ إِلَيْهِمْ عَهْدَهُمْ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"Cast thou from thee, to them, their covenant;"]," i. e. ",[1,"reject it,"]," or ",[1,"renounce it, to them"],"]. (Bd in viii. 60.) And ",[2,"هٰذَا"]," ↓ ",[2,"اِطَّرِحْ"],[2,"الحَدِيثَ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"Dismiss thou this discourse"],"]. (A, TA. [See the pass. part. n., below.]) And ↓ ",[2,"اِطَّرِحْ"],[2,"شُكْرِى وَلَوْمِى"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Let thou alone,"]," or ",[1,"abstain thou from, thanking me and blaming me."]," (Har p. 332.) -A2- ",[2,"طَرِحَ"],", (IAar, O, K,) aor. , (K,) inf. n. ",[2,"طَرَحٌ"],", (TK,) ",[1,"He"]," (a man, IAar, O) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, evil in disposition."]," (IAar, O, K.) ― -b2- And ",[1,"He enjoyed,"]," or ",[1,"led, a life of ample ease and comfort."]," (IAar, O, K.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"طَرَّحَ","t":["see 1. ― -b2- ",[2,"طرّح"],", (S, A, O, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَطْرِيحٌ"],", (S, K,) signifies also (tropical:) ",[1,"He made"]," a thing ",[1,"long,"]," or ",[1,"he made"]," it ",[1,"high:"]," (TA:) or ",[1,"he made"]," his building ",[1,"long;"]," (S, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"طَرْمَحَ"],", (S, and K in art. ",[2,"طرمح"],",) in which the ",[2,"م"]," is [said to be] augmentative: (S:) or both signify ",[1,"he made"]," his building ",[1,"long and high:"]," (A:) or the former signifies ",[1,"he made"]," his building ",[1,"very long."]," (O.) ― -b3- And ",[1,"He"]," (a horse) ",[1,"took long,"]," or ",[1,"wide, steps in running."]," (O, TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"مُطَارَحَةُ الكَلَامِ","t":["is a phrase well known: (S, K:) ",[2,"المُطَارَحَةُ"]," signifies (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The bandying of words, one with another;"]," (KL, and Har p. 190;) ",[1,"the holding a colloquy,"]," or ",[1,"a discussion, with another:"]," and it is [said to be] primarily used in relation to singing. (Har ibid.) You say; ",[2,"طارحهُ الكَلَامَ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He held a colloquy,"]," or ",[1,"a discussion, with him."]," (MA.) And ",[2,"طَارَحْتُهُ العِلْمَ"]," and ",[2,"الغِنَآءَ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"I bandied with him scientific discourse"]," and ",[1,"songs"],"]. (A.) [See also 6.]"],"f":"3"},{"h":"أَطْرِح","t":["(tropical:) ",[1,"Look thou:"]," (A, TA:) from ",[2,"طَرْفٌ"],[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"]," and ",[2,"طَرِيحٌ"],". (TA.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"تطرّح","t":[[1,"He attired himself with a"],[2,"طَرْحَة"],": a post-classical word.]"],"f":"5"},{"h":"تطارحوا","t":["(tropical:) ",[1,"They bandied questions, one with another; put,"]," or ",[1,"proposed,"]," (lit. ",[1,"threw,"],") ",[1,"questions, one to another."]," (A.)"],"f":"6"},{"h":"اِطَّرَحَ","t":[": see 1, in three places."],"f":"8"},{"h":"طَرْمَحَ","t":[": see 2; and see also art. ",[2,"طرمح"],"."],"f":"Q. Q. 1"},{"h":"طِرْحٌ","t":["(S, A, K) and ↓ ",[2,"طُرَّحٌ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"طَرِيحٌ"]," (K) A thing (S, A) ",[1,"cast, thrown,"]," or ",[1,"flung, away,"]," syn. ",[2,"مَطْرُوحٌ"],", (S, A, K,) ",[1,"and not wanted by any one."]," (S.) One says, ",[2,"لَوْ بَاتَ مَتَاعُكَ طِرْحًا مَا أُخِذَ"]," [",[1,"If thy household goods passed the night,"]," or ",[1,"remained during the night, cast away and neglected, they would not be taken"],"]. (A, TA.) -A2- And ",[2,"طِرْحٌ"]," signifies also The ",[1,"leopard:"]," so says Aboo-Kheyreh: pl. ",[2,"طُرُوحٌ"],". (O.)"]},{"h":"طَرَحٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Distance,"]," or ",[1,"remoteness."]," (TA.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"طَرُوحٌ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"طَرْحَةٌ","t":["The [",[1,"article of apparel called"],"] ",[2,"طَيْلَسَان"]," [q. v.]: (O, K:) it was not known to the Arabs. (O.) [See De Sacy's Chrest. Arabe, sec. ed., ii. 267-269: and Dozy's Dict. des Noms des Vêtements chez les Arabes, pp. 254-262. It is now applied in Egypt to a kind of head-veil worn by women, the two ends of which generally hang down behind, nearly reaching to the ground: but it is often worn in another manner; about a quarter of it hanging down behind, and the remainder being turned over the head, and under the chin, and over the head again, so that the middle part covers the bosom, and both ends hang down behind: it is a piece of muslin, or the like, often embroidered at each end; about three quarters of a yard in width, and in length nearly equal to twice the height of the wearer.]"]},{"h":"طُرَّحٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"طِرْحٌ"],"."]},{"h":"طَرَاحٌ","t":[": see the next paragraph."]},{"h":"طَرُوحٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A distant"]," place; as also ↓ ",[2,"طَرَحٌ"],", (S, K,) and ↓ ",[2,"طَرَاحٌ"],", (K,) and [app. ↓ ",[2,"طَارِحٌ"],", for] one says ",[2,"دِيَارٌ طَوَارِحُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"Distant dwellings"]," or ",[1,"abodes"]," [as though the latter word were pl. of ",[2,"طَارِحَةٌ"],"]. (A, TA.) [Hence,] ",[2,"عُقْبَةٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"A stage of a journey"],"] ",[1,"far-extending."]," (A, * O: in a copy of the former ",[2,"عَقَبَةٌ"],".) And ↓ ",[2,"سَيْرٌ طُرَاحِىٌّ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A far,"]," or ",[1,"distant, journey:"]," (As, S, O, K:) or ",[1,"a hard journey."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"نِيَّةٌ طَرُوحٌ"],", (TA,) or ↓ ",[2,"طَرَحٌ"],", (T, K, TA, and O in art. ",[2,"ضرح"],",) like ",[2,"ضَرَحٌ"],", (O in that art.,) ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"بَعِيدَةٌ"]," [app. meaning (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A distant,"]," or ",[1,"remote, thing,"]," or ",[1,"place, that is the object of an action"]," or ",[1,"a journey"],"]. (T, O, K.) And ",[2,"نَخْلَةٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A palm-tree having long racemes:"]," (S, O, K:) or ",[1,"of which the upper part is far from the lower:"]," pl. ",[2,"طُرُحٌ"],", with two dammehs. (TA.) ― -b2- ",[2,"قَوْسٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A bow that propels the arrow with vehemence;"]," (S, A, O;) ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"ضَرُوحٌ"],": (S, O, K:) or ",[1,"that sends the arrow far:"]," (TA:) or ",[1,"that sends it to the furthest limit."]," (AHn, TA.) And ",[2,"رَجُلٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A man who, when he compresses, impregnates."]," (Lh, O, K.) And ",[2,"فَحْلٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"],", q. v. (O.) And ",[2,"زَمَنٌ طَرُوحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A time that casts the people thereof into places,"]," or ",[1,"positions, of peril:"]," and ",[2,"نَوَائِبُ طُرْحٌ"]," [or ",[2,"طُرُحٌ"],", as above, (tropical:) ",[1,"Accidents that cast people into such places"]," or ",[1,"positions"],"]. (A.)"]},{"h":"طَرِيحٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"طِرْحٌ"],": ― -b2- and see also ",[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"],"."]},{"h":"سَيْرٌ طُرَاحِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"طَرُوحٌ"],"."]},{"h":"طَرَّاحَةٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"],"."]},{"h":"طَارِحٌ","t":[": [fem. with ",[2,"ة"],"; and pl. of the latter ",[2,"طَوَارِحُ"],":] see ",[2,"طَرُوحٌ"],"."]},{"h":"سَنَامٌ إِطْرِيحٌ","t":[[1,"A long,"]," (S, O, L, K,) or ",[1,"tall,"]," (S, * O, * L, K, *) ",[1,"camel's hump,"]," (S, O, L, K,) ",[1,"leaning on one side."]," (L.) [See an ex. voce ",[2,"إِسْلِيحٌ"],".]"]},{"h":"أُطْرُوحَةٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A question that one puts,"]," or ",[1,"proposes,"]," lit. ",[1,"throws."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"فُلَانٌ يُلْقِى الأَطَارِيحَ","t":["is expl. by AO as meaning ",[1,"Such a ones moves both his arms up and down"]," [",[1,"in walking"],"]: denoting a proud and self-conceited manner of walking. (O.)"]},{"h":"مَطْرَحٌ","t":[[1,"A place where,"]," or ",[1,"into which, a thing"]," [or ",[1,"person is cast"]," or ",[1,"thrown"]," or] ",[1,"is made to be:"]," pl. ",[2,"مَطَارِحُ"],". (Har p. 188.) ― -b2- [And hence,] (tropical:) ",[1,"A state in which a person is"]," [",[1,"put,"]," or ",[1,"placed"],"]: so in the saying, ",[2,"مَاطَرَحَكَ هٰذَا المَطْرَحَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"What hath put,"]," or ",[1,"placed, thee in this state"]," in which thou art? (A.)"]},{"h":"مِطْرَحٌ","t":[[1,"I. q."],[2,"مِفْرَشٌ"]," [q. v.: and ↓ ",[2,"طَرَّاحَةٌ"]," has the same, or a similar, meaning; applied in the present day to ",[1,"a horse-cloth,"]," and ",[1,"the like;"]," and to ",[1,"a mattress"],"]: pl. ",[2,"مَطَارِحُ"],". (A, TA.) ― -b2- ",[2,"فَحْلٌ"],[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A stallion that sends his semen far into the womb;"]," (A, * O, K;) like ↓ ",[2,"طَرُوحٌ"],". (O.) And ",[2,"طَرْفٌ مِطْرَحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"An eye that sees far;"]," (A, O, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"طَرِيحٌ"],". (A, TA.) And ",[2,"رُمْحٌ"],[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A long spear."]," (A, K.) And ",[2,"إِبِلٌ مَطَارِحُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"Quick,"]," or ",[1,"swift, camels."]," (A, TA.) ― -b3- [",[2,"مِطْرَحٌ"],", as stated by Freytag, is also expl. by Reiske as meaning ",[1,"Camela in cujus ventrem aqua profunda cadit:"]," but this explanation may have originated from a doubtful instance of the same epithet applied to a stallion camel: see above.]"]},{"h":"قَوْلٌ مُطَّرَحٌ","t":["(tropical:) ",[1,"A"]," [",[1,"rejected"],"] ",[1,"saying, to which no regard is paid."]," (A, TA.)"]},{"h":"مَشَى مُتَطَرِّحًا","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He walked,"]," or ",[1,"went, in a slack,"]," or ",[1,"languid, manner; as though repeatedly stumbling,"]," or ",[1,"throwing himself down;"]," syn. ",[2,"مُتَسَاقِطًا"],"; (IDrd, A, O;) ",[1,"like one fatigued,"]," or ",[1,"weary,"]," (IDrd, O, K,) ",[1,"and weak."]," (TA.)"]}]},"maqayis":["الطاء والراء والحاء أصل صحيح يدل على نبذ الشيء وإلقائه. يقال: طرح الشيء يطرحه طرحا. ومن ذلك الطرح، وهو المكان البعيد. وطرحت النوى بفلان كل مطرح، إذا نأت به ورمت به. قال: ألما بمي قبل أن تطرح النوى ... بنا مطرحا أو قبل بين يزيلها ويقال: فحل مطرح ; بعيد موقع الماء في الرحم. ومن الباب: نخلة طروح: طويلة العراجين. وسنام إطريح: طويل. وقوس طروح: شديدة الحفز للسهم. والقياس في كله واحد."],"mufradat":["الطرح: إلقاء الشيء وإبعاده، والطروح: المكان البعيد، ورأيته من طرح أي: بعد، والطرح: المطروح لقلة الاعتداد به. قال تعالى: اقتلوا يوسف أو اطرحوه أرضا [يوسف/ 9] ."]}